  "assembly_observations": [
    "VADDExec original and baseline use the same 12-byte frame and four-lane loop. Original carry evaluation precedes selector/address evaluation; the baseline evaluates the selector first. Result and persistent pointer registers differ. Saturation branch predicates and all observed arithmetic operations agree.",
    "RSP_MixAudio baseline matches the entire original suffix at offsets 0xC8 through 0x27F; all 169 differing bytes are in its initialization prefix. A setup-only match is not a complete-function match.",
    "RSP_WriteCOP0 original initializes destination before source in each transfer direction. Its first direction uses EDI for SP destination and ESI for RAM source; the second direction uses EDI for RAM destination and EBX for SP source. This is a source-order clue, not proof of original variable names."
  ],
